.TH FILELRC 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
filelrc \- Extracts audio metadata and fetches track lyrics via lrcget
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filelrc
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fImode\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput_file\fR] \fIaudio_file\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filelrc
is a command-line utility that automates the lyrics lookup process for local audio files. It checks for local dependencies, uses \fBffprobe\fR to parse the targeted media file, and normalizes its internal metadata tags to extract the track name, artist name, album name, and runtime duration.
.PP
Once the track name and artist name are validated, it passes all available parameters downstream to \fBlrcget\fR. If album or duration tags are missing from the file, the underlying query automatically downgrades to a broader search query instead of failing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show the help menu and exit.
.TP
.B \-m \fImode\fR
Specify the parsing structure passed downstream to \fBlrcget\fR. Valid targets include:
.RS
.IP "\fBjson\fR" 12
Returns the raw JSON response payload from the API.
.IP "\fBsynced\fR" 12
Extracts timed LRC-formatted lyrics only.
.IP "\fBplain\fR" 12
Extracts plain text lyrics without timestamps.
.IP "\fBfallback\fR" 12
Attempts to extract synced lyrics first; if unavailable, falls back to plain text.
.RE
.TP
.B \-o \fIoutput_file\fR
Saves the processed output stream into the designated target file instead of redirecting it to stdout.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I audio_file
The path to the local audio file containing embedded metadata tags to be parsed. Track title and artist tags must be present.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure due to missing dependencies, unreadable files, missing required track name or artist tags, or invalid flags.
.PP
Note: Exit codes 2, 3, and 4 may be bubbled up directly from the underlying execution of \fBlrcget\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.B filelrc \-m synced \-o song_lyrics.lrc track01.flac
.RS
Probes track01.flac for metadata, then passes those variables to lrcget to extract synced lyrics into song_lyrics.lrc.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lrcget (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR jq (1)
